For this graph, the adjacency list therefore the matrix, BFS/DFS must scan an entire row to determine which vertices are adjacent. uses considerably less storage than the 36-entry matrix.

Traversal behaviour
Feature	Adjacency Matrix	Adjacency List
BFS	O(V²)	O(V + E)
DFS	O(V²)	O(V + E)
Find all neighbours of a vertex	O(V)	O(degree(v))
Check whether an edge exists	O(1)	O(degree(v))
Space	O(V²)	O(V + E)

With the matrix, BFS/DFS must scan an entire row to determine which vertices are adjacent. Thus, even if a vertex has only two neighbours, up to V matrix entries may be examined.

With the adjacency list, only the actual neighbours are examined for every possible pair of vertices.

Overall analysis
This social network is sparse because there are relatively few connections compared with the maximum possible number of connections.

For an undirected graph with 6 vertices, the maximum number of edges is:

